# resiliency-saga/ — the ten-chapter epic

Ten ordered `.feature` files, one per chapter of the narrative described in this
directory's `README.md`. Each chapter file carries exactly one `@concern:saga-NN-<name>`
tag (registered in `../README.md`'s concern taxonomy table) and reuses existing
step definitions from `steps/dataplane.steps.ts` and `steps/resilience.steps.ts`
wherever a fitting primitive already exists; new glue lives in
`steps/dataplane/resiliency-saga.steps.ts`.

**Considered, no enforcing rule beyond the parent's.** This manifest exists to satisfy
the parent `genesis/a2o/.epr-meta` no-orphan-subtree rule (`new-feature-subdir-needs-meta`)
and to claim coverage (`covers: subtree`) so the coverage walk terminates here. The real
authoring discipline — tag requirements, RED-FIRST assertions, step-definition placement —
is prose convention in the parent `CLAUDE.md`/`README.md`, not a mechanizable predicate; no
new drift has been observed in this tree that a rule would catch better than review.
